  "id": "Compound::DB00880 - Gene::759",
  "verbalization": "Chlorothiazide, a thiazide diuretic, is consistently linked to the binding of Ca1 through multiple pathways in the hetionet dataset. The evidence suggests that Chlorothiazide is included in the class of thiazide diuretics, which in turn bind Ca1. This relationship is supported by multiple paths, including those involving Bendroflumethiazide and Methyclothiazide, both of which are subtypes of thiazide diuretics and bind Ca1. The lowest common ancestors across these paths indicate a shared biological context, reinforcing the mechanistic link between Chlorothiazide and Ca1. The integration of these pathways suggests that thiazide diuretics may modulate calcium signaling through a common mechanism, potentially affecting cellular processes involving calcium homeostasis. The evidence is robust and consistent, supporting a direct interaction between Chlorothiazide and Ca1, mediated through thiazide diuretic class relationships.",
